I've written the session plan: two task files in session_plan/, plus issue_responses.md. The commit step didn't actually commit anything because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the files exist on disk only. The harness reads them from there.

Task 1 — Part of #1023 (tools/fence, product). Since yoagent 0.25.5, ripgrep (the rg search program) ignores the user's config file. But src/fence_result_filter.rs still says a ripgrep config can reshape output, in two places: the module doc and unattributed_note(), a message the model sees when the fence withholds lines. The task is:
• Confirm the upgrade's behaviour in yoagent's search.rs.
• Work out which output shapes can still hit the branch that withholds lines the fence can't tie to a file, and keep that branch.
• Rewrite both sentences and add a yoagent-version-claim marker, so the next upgrade forces a re-read.
• Pin the new note text with a test on the exact string the model receives.
• Mark the old claim as superseded in ARCHITECTURE.md.

It's titled "Part of" because #1023's items 2 (the (N matches) count includes withheld lines) and 3 (find warnings pass denied path names) stay open.

Task 2 — Part of #982 (watch/dispatch, product). Two commands print a usage message but exit 0, so a script reads success:
• yoyo watch lint when no lint command is detected. This copies the 14:31 fix for bare watch (2b5a5c17).
